]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Plan-review remediation (2026-08-07)\n\nThe first review BLOCKED because the consumer inventory was incomplete. The plan of record now includes these additional edits:\n\n- `src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py`: remove the `BRIDGE_STATUS` export, constant, and `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS[\"bridge_status\"]` entry together with `bridge_status.schema.json`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py`: replace both live `Run: ticket bridge-status for details.` warnings with neutral guidance to inspect unresolved bridge alerts. Do not point at `bridge status` because that sibling command has not landed yet.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/output.py`: remove `bridge-status` from the report-profile documentation.\n- `docs/output-schemas.md`: remove the `bridge-status` to `bridge_status` row.\n- `CHANGELOG.md`: add the two retirement release notes. Existing historical entries remain intentionally.\n\nThe B6 oracle is exact: a behavioral contract test proves both retired CLI tokens are unknown and absent from top-level help, then asserts zero `bridge-status` or `purge-bridge` matches in the shipped package tree `src/rebar` and the active command-contract docs `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, and `docs/output-schemas.md`. Tests, `CHANGELOG.md`, and `docs/archive` are excluded because they intentionally retain specification or historical evidence.\n\nSupplemental acceptance criteria, split for independent verification:\n\n- [ ] `rebar bridge-status` exits as an unknown command.\n- [ ] `rebar purge-bridge` exits as an unknown command.\n- [ ] Neither retired command appears in `rebar --help`.\n- [ ] The schema registry has no `BRIDGE_STATUS` export, constant, or output-schema entry.\n- [ ] Both surviving read warnings provide neutral bridge-alert guidance and name no retired or not-yet-shipped command.\n- [ ] The shipped-package and active-doc zero-match oracle passes.\n- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` records both retirements.","timestamp":1786117752761983001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan-review remediation: direct grep confirmed the dangling `epic 3a03` citation at `src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge.py:6`, while unrelated surviving citations also exist in `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py`. Narrowed the current acceptance criterion to deletion of the retired module citation, added an explicit straight-revert rollback path, and recorded the surviving test citations as discovered task `2380-e9b7-0d7c-4d0f` linked `discovered_from` this ticket.","timestamp":1786118678885356001}],"created_at":1786095480764283001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9a4f707c-4d85-44db-8012-581bb175b2af","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f5c3-e7e3-cce1-4eca"},{"link_uuid":"17a425c6-cda6-4818-92c2-7b9ac06b42f3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4f2b-daef-2f9b-4aaa"},{"link_uuid":"11d2888b-bd51-4e81-85d0-81266f2d574e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"70fa-5b4d-c9c2-44ee"},{"link_uuid":"e60b3f5a-120e-4f29-8e2e-17c50b3b76e5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b44b-9743-da44-4cfa"},{"link_uuid":"3bbcf48a-a3b1-44a5-b3f9-19bf86cb85a5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ae60-907b-9c7f-4b90"}],"description":"## Context and intent\n\nRetire the two bridge verbs that were dead on arrival: `rebar bridge-status` and\n`rebar purge-bridge`. This pure dead-code deletion was carved out of\n`4752-3afb-e8bd-448a` so it could land independently; nothing in the new `bridge`\nsurface replaces either verb.\n\n`bridge-status` consumed `<tracker>/.bridge-status.json`, but this repository never\ncontained a producer and the command exited 1 on post-cutover repositories. Its module\nalso carried a dangling `epic 3a03` citation. `purge-bridge` had no script, workflow,\nor runbook caller and exposed an inverted-sense `--keep` flag. Neither command warranted\na compatibility alias or deprecation forwarder.\n\n## Completed implementation\n\nGerrit change 1517 (`Ic40ab04419a5ebfb4e0b6486cb1272309f4dfc67`) merged to\n`main` on 2026-08-07 after `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and zero unresolved\ncomments. The merged implementation has these observable end states:\n\n- CLI wiring in `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` contains only the surviving\n  `bridge-fsck` entry in `_BRIDGE`; the `bridge-status` and `purge-bridge` dispatch\n  arms are absent. Top-level `rebar doctor` remains unchanged.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge.py` and\n  `src/rebar/_commands/purge_bridge.py` are absent, with no shims or aliases.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge-status.txt`,\n  `src/rebar/_cli/help/purge-bridge.txt`, and both overview entries are absent.\n- `src/rebar/schemas/bridge_status.schema.json`, the `BRIDGE_STATUS` export and\n  constant, and the `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS[\"bridge_status\"]` entry are absent.\n- The retired-only tests are absent:\n  `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_status.py`,\n  `tests/unit/test_purge_bridge_locked_commit.py`,\n  `tests/interfaces/store/test_purge_bridge_prune_concurrency.py`, and\n  `tests/interfaces/store/_purge_race_worker.py`.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_coverage.py` has no retired schema\n  exemption. `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py` asserts both\n  tokens are retired. `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_alert_display.py` positively\n  verifies neutral guidance from both surviving bridge-alert warning paths.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py` names no retired or not-yet-shipped\n  command, and `src/rebar/_engine_support/output.py` no longer documents a\n  `bridge-status` report profile.\n- Active command documentation was updated in `docs/cli-reference.md`,\n  `docs/exit-codes.md`, and `docs/output-schemas.md`.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` records the breaking removals. `docs/release-notes.md` is an\n  enumerated, intentional consumer: it records the agent-visible removal of both\n  commands and the `bridge_status` output schema. Those historical retirement names\n  are expected there and are not stale live-surface references.\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` carries the resulting shrink of `_dispatch`.\n\nNo persisted ticket data, migration, external integration, auth boundary, or shared\nstate format changed.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\n- Held-out retirement contract: 7/7 tests passed. Restoring `bridge-status` made the\n  oracle fail, and the refactoring litmus passed.\n- Focused post-rebase contracts: 41 passed across help, schema, and alert-display tests.\n- Local gates: `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed across 437 source files.\n- Full pre-rebase suite: 11,149 passed, 40 skipped, 228 deselected.\n- Exact patch-set-2 CI run 31218769114 passed artifact provenance, optionality,\n  dependency audit, identity, ticket resolution, golden path, lint/typecheck, and all\n  macOS/Ubuntu Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 test matrices.\n- The behavioral oracle proves both retired tokens take the unknown-command path and\n  are absent from top-level help. Live package and command-contract surfaces contain\n  no `bridge-status` or `purge-bridge` references. Tests, changelogs, archives, and the\n  explicit retirement notice in `docs/release-notes.md` retain intentional history.\n\n## Rollback\n\nIf an undiscovered downstream consumer still invokes either retired verb, revert\nGerrit change 1517. No data migration or persisted-format reversal is required.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar bridge-status` exits as an unknown command.\n- [x] `rebar purge-bridge` exits as an unknown command.\n- [x] Neither retired command appears in `rebar --help`.\n- [x] Both implementation modules are deleted without shims or aliases.\n- [x] The retired schema and every `BRIDGE_STATUS` registry surface are absent.\n- [x] Surviving read warnings provide neutral bridge-alert guidance.\n- [x] The package/help/active-command-doc oracle passes, with historical evidence\n      explicitly scoped and retained.\n- [x] Retired-only tests are deleted and replacement behavioral contracts pass.\n- [x] Active command docs, `CHANGELOG.md`, and `docs/release-notes.md` record the\n      correct post-removal contract.\n- [x] The dangling `epic 3a03` citation disappeared with its retired module.\n- [x] `bridge-fsck` and top-level `rebar doctor` behavior remain intact.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"drop bridge-status and purge-bridge from the _BRIDGE frozenset (~121) and delete both dispatch arms (~305, ~312)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge.py","reason":"the bridge-status implementation module retires whole, including its _USAGE string (line 32) and the dangling epic 3a03 docstring citation"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/purge_bridge.py","reason":"the purge-bridge implementation retires whole, including its stale ticket-purge-bridge.sh _USAGE string (line 37)"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/bridge_status.schema.json","reason":"schema retired with the verb; b69c publishes its own status schema"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge-status.txt","reason":"help page for a retired verb"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/purge-bridge.txt","reason":"help page for a retired verb"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt","reason":"remove the bridge-status and purge-bridge lines from rebar --help"},{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_status.py","reason":"covers only the retired bridge-status verb; deleted with it"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_purge_bridge_locked_commit.py","reason":"covers only the retired purge-bridge verb; deleted with it"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_purge_bridge_prune_concurrency.py","reason":"purge-bridge deletion-commit concurrency regression; deleted with the verb"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/_purge_race_worker.py","reason":"standalone worker driving purge_bridge_cli for the concurrency test; deleted with it"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_coverage.py","reason":"drop the bridge-status EXEMPT_BRIDGE entry (~125) now that the schema is gone"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","reason":"verb inventory must no longer expect the retired verbs"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"remove the purge-bridge (~324) and bridge-status sections"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"remove the bridge-status (79) and purge-bridge (101) rows"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py","reason":"remove BRIDGE_STATUS export, constant, and OUTPUT_SCHEMAS registry entry with the deleted schema"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py","reason":"replace two live warnings that direct users to the retired bridge-status verb with neutral bridge-alert guidance"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/output.py","reason":"remove bridge-status from the report-profile documentation"},{"path":"docs/output-schemas.md","reason":"remove the bridge-status to bridge_status mapping for the retired command and schema"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"release notes record both command retirements while preserving historical entries"},{"path":".github/complexity-baseline.json","reason":"shrink the _dispatch complexity ceiling after deleting the two dispatch arms"},{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_alert_display.py","reason":"positively assert the neutral guidance emitted by both surviving bridge-alert warning paths"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"record the breaking agent-visible CLI contract removal and migration behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3"],["relates_to","4f2b-daef-2f9b-4aaa"],["relates_to","70fa-5b4d-c9c2-44ee"],["relates_to","ae60-907b-9c7f-4b90"],["relates_to","b44b-9743-da44-4cfa"],["relates_to","f5c3-e7e3-cce1-4eca"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3","parent_status_uuid":"b6fc41bf-6df0-4cdb-809b-4232639efd2e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bridge","ux"],"ticket_id":"c61a-9f8f-8ef9-4601","ticket_type":"task","title":"Retire the two dead bridge verbs (bridge-status, purge-bridge)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["23e1d243-5a70-409e-affc-aa3a696026e4","ee9c9406-8cd0-4b35-91d3-d3680918146c","09709000-724a-4d2f-9698-9afd30365241","3c887ed0-4e80-4a55-b969-284e7d287a1e","3282a212-bf25-4ec5-b87f-e04e0ed51c8a","b2d217b0-c3b6-4b59-807d-c4223319fb60","d6506dc2-e3c9-4d58-a64e-f5002f20cac4","d8237720-8a61-44d1-b6ed-2ddf95f75728","08248385-03c6-4938-affc-d7b605faad8b","b6fc41bf-6df0-4cdb-809b-4232639efd2e","d120e7ff-0ac7-43f8-91b6-4524769dc1c4","ab18cde1-1be9-435a-ab6a-b368cfca7cba","9a4f707c-4d85-44db-8012-581bb175b2af","06848c59-dffd-4341-9b2a-2aaca9f5729b","17a425c6-cda6-4818-92c2-7b9ac06b42f3","7d22688a-ce41-48db-8246-e4907ed92ded","11d2888b-bd51-4e81-85d0-81266f2d574e","e60b3f5a-120e-4f29-8e2e-17c50b3b76e5","3bbcf48a-a3b1-44a5-b3f9-19bf86cb85a5","ceb90b27-b74b-4f52-9207-ad7ed4904485"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786139354661613002,"uuid":"ecce40e4-39f2-4732-97c5-702b8a479675"}